    "sha": "252d53306578476143b8ef60c11afdd3ffa610e6",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDI1MmQ1MzMwNjU3ODQ3NjE0M2I4ZWY2MGMxMWFmZGQzZmZhNjEwZTY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T23:50:38Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T23:50:38Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): G76 threading cycle on the Fanuc Lathe post from a thread-cycle record\n\nThe thread kernel now carries one cl::ThreadCycle beside its explicit\npasses (start, root end, major/minor diameter, lead, height, first and\nminimum depth, finish allowance, infeed angle, spring passes, pull-out,\nand the move span it stands for). The sim and verify keep reading the\npasses; the record rides the stream as THREAD ... / THREAD END around\nthem and the project cache as an additive `threads` key.\n\nA new document singleton PostOptions (undoable SetPostOptions, a\n\"Threading\" combo under the post picker while Fanuc Lathe is chosen,\npersisted as an additive `post_options` key) reaches the script as\nthe global `postOptions` via engine::run_with. Fanuc Lathe with\nThreading = G76 writes the two-block G76 (P m r a Q dmin R d /\nX Z P k Q d F lead) from the record and skips the passes; the default\nstays G32, so every existing golden is byte-identical, and posts\nwithout onThreadCycle ignore the record. Under G76, passes without a\nrecord or a record out of range are refused by name.\n\nGolden: crates/app/tests/golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/thread_g76.nc.\nPinned by lathe_post_g76 (golden, G32 default unchanged, stream and\nproject round trip, refusals, option undo) and motion\nturning_thread_cycle.\n\nFixes #34\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
